The books in books/ and their covers in image/covers are Standard Ebooks editions (https://standardebooks.org). The
texts and cover paintings are in the US public domain, and Standard Ebooks dedicates its own work on them to the public
domain under CC0 1.0 (https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/). Their descriptions on the book pages come
from the same editions. Copyright laws differ between countries; check yours before relying on a book being free there.

Word meanings in the reader are fetched as you ask for them from Wiktionary (https://en.wiktionary.org), whose text is
available under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 License; each one says so where it is shown. Book pages
link to free LibriVox recordings (https://librivox.org), which LibriVox releases into the public domain.

The two Alice books, Alice's Adventures in Wonderland and Through the Looking-Glass, are Standard Ebooks editions
with Tenniel's illustrations kept at their ordinary resolution only (Standard Ebooks also includes copies at double
resolution); their text is unchanged. Accounts, when they are switched on, are run on Google's Firebase.

